  "body": "Replace sampler dtype and strided copies with registered TileLang kernels, using vector loads and a column-first grid for aligned inputs. Large aligned FP32 copies use native pitched CUDA DMA; dense FP32 retains DMA. General layouts use TileLang without an ATen compute fallback. Sampling order, masks, raw-logit preservation and RNG stay unchanged.\n\nThe revised candidate passes all 18 GPU timing cases on both boots under a zero-margin, five-standard-error gate, with exact program/binding equality for unchanged DMA. Both boots pass 120 tests, including live graph payloads and side streams. The 96-row padded FP32 case is now about 2% faster. Historical regressions and rejected alternatives are preserved.\n\nFresh patch application reproduces the source tree; all three files match the composed qualified source. Doctor and diff checks pass. Built-image and full serving qualification remain; no promoted config or serving process changed. See `experiments/2026-11-05-sampler-copy-performance` for the selected series, strict gates and evidence links.\n",
